WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:08.000
Self-custody works until the only key holder becomes unavailable. Heirloom adds a precommitted USDC continuity plan on Base.

00:08.000 --> 00:17.000
The owner connects with a wallet or passkey-backed Base Account and remains in control while active.

00:17.000 --> 00:29.000
This verified Base Sepolia vault holds twenty USDC. Its owner, asset, routes, guardians, and deadlines are reconstructed from public contract reads.

00:29.000 --> 00:40.000
Fresh owner-authorized actions reset liveness. After ninety days of inactivity and a seven-day challenge window, distribution becomes irreversible.

00:40.000 --> 00:49.000
Any caller may execute the plan, but the contract, not the caller, derives the recipient, amount, and valid time phase.

00:49.000 --> 00:57.000
Fallback eligibility is time-based; Heirloom does not detect death or lost keys. Evidence includes seventy-three tests, five stateful groups, and sixteen of sixteen killed mutants.

00:57.000 --> 01:00.000
Heirloom: permissionless execution without payout authority, built for Base.
